# Installation Guide — eSawda v{{VERSION}}

This guide sets up the **backend** (Laravel API) and the **frontend** (Next.js).
Estimated time: ~20–30 minutes.

## 0. Requirements

| Component | Version |
|-----------|---------|
| PHP       | 8.2 or newer (with `pdo_mysql`, `mbstring`, `gd`, `zip`) |
| Composer  | 2.x |
| MySQL / MariaDB | 8.0 / 10.6+ |
| Node.js   | 20 LTS or newer |
| npm       | 10+ |

---

## 1. Backend (Laravel API)

```bash
cd backend
cp .env.example .env
composer install --optimize-autoloader
php artisan key:generate
```

Edit `.env` and set at minimum:

```
APP_URL=https://api.your-domain.com
DB_DATABASE=esawda
DB_USERNAME=your_db_user
DB_PASSWORD=your_db_password
FRONTEND_URL=https://your-domain.com
```

Create the database, then build the schema with migrations:

```bash
php artisan migrate --seed
```

This creates every table and seeds the default data (admin account, plans,
etc.). Re-run with `php artisan migrate:fresh --seed` to start clean.

Link storage and serve:

```bash
php artisan storage:link
php artisan serve   # or point your web server at public/
```

---

## 2. Frontend (Next.js)

```bash
cd frontend
cp .env.local.example .env.local
npm install
```

Edit `.env.local`:

```
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE=https://api.your-domain.com
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-domain.com
```

Run it:

```bash
npm run dev          # development
# production:
npm run build && npm run start
```

---

## 3. Production notes

- Serve the backend `public/` folder via Nginx/Apache; keep `storage/` writable.
- Run the frontend with a process manager (PM2 / systemd) behind Nginx.
- Set up the queue worker: `php artisan queue:work` (or Horizon).
- Schedule the cron: `* * * * * php artisan schedule:run`.

See `docs/deployment-guide.md` for a full production walkthrough.

---

## 4. Default admin

After seeding, log in to the admin panel with the credentials printed by the
seeder (change them immediately in production).

